// What a receiver saw on its latest step.
//
// Only what a non-blocking receive can actually observe. There is no `CLOSED`:
// UDP has no connection, so a sender that went away looks exactly like a
// sender with nothing to say, and the receiver reports that as `NO_DATA` while
// its `age` output grows. A consumer that needs "the link is down" thresholds
// `age`.
//
//   NO_DATA     nothing arrived this step; the data output still holds the
//               last datagram
//   RECEIVED    at least one datagram arrived, and the last one fit. A
//               zero-length datagram is RECEIVED with size 0, not a close
//   TRUNCATED   the last datagram was larger than the receiver's capacity;
//               the data output holds its first `capacity` bytes, and is
//               therefore not the whole message
//   ERROR       the receive failed; the log names the reason once, when the
//               status first becomes ERROR
package se.net;

finite RxStatus { NO_DATA, RECEIVED, TRUNCATED, ERROR }
